  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the least probable outcome of each lottery (i.e., the best outcome, as both lotteries only have one positive outcome) and prefers the one with the higher payoff. The individual considered exactly this: the best possible outcome of each lottery, acknowledging their low and differing probabilities, and chose based on which offered the higher gain in that rare event. The individual’s justification aligns with the rule of the decision reason: when probabilities are both very low, pick the one with the better payoff in that least likely (but best) case. There is strong correspondence between the information used (the best outcome and its low likelihood) and the rule (favoring the better such outcome). The verbal report reflects a clear reliance on the decision reason.",
  "final_assessment_score": 100
